# L §3.1: none "can only be tested, with x == none or x != none; any other comparison, arithmetic, ordering
# or aggregation of it is refused (RUN-NONE). A row, a field or a rule may give none ... A def whose winning
# rule gives none ... prints none (D-7)."
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"

input x: int
input y: int

def z: int at reader
  rule base = none

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x = none
  y = 2

ask q1: x == none, x != none, y == none
ask q2: x + y
ask q3: x < y
ask q4: z law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: (true, false, false)
  cut 2026-01-01
q2: refused: RUN-NONE ...
  cut 2026-01-01
q3: refused: RUN-NONE ...
  cut 2026-01-01
q4: none
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
